# Doxygen-input documentation uses @ref cross-references whose targets contain
# underscores (e.g. `@ref PC::send_template`). Prettier parses those
# underscores as Markdown emphasis and rewrites them to `*`, which silently
# breaks the Doxygen links. These files are therefore excluded from Prettier;
# GitHub-facing Markdown (README.md, docs/CHANGELOG.md, …) is still formatted.
docs/README.md
docs/RFC.md
docs/SECURITY.md
docs/SSH.md
docs/TODO.md
test/README.md

# Generated data: the compiler dependency graph is written by ci_tooling/generate/gen_dep_graph.py (compact
# json.dump) and regenerated verbatim by CI; Prettier would reformat it and cause churn.
test/dep_graph.json
# Likewise the SonarQube compile-commands baseline (ci_tooling/sonar/merge_compiledb.py json.dump,
# @ROOT@-tokenized); affected runs overlay it verbatim, so keep Prettier off it.
test/compile_commands.json

# The two matrices are spliced, never re-rendered: a mutation goes through a subcommand that edits
# the text in place so the diff names the one env it changed. A whole-file reformat is valid JSON
# and moves all 400 of them, which is exactly what the harnesses refuse to do.
test/test_matrix.json
test/performance_benching/bench_matrix.json

# Ratchet baselines, written by ci_tooling/lib/baseline.py json.dump. Prettier reformats them and
# the next `ci.py baseline` writes them back, so the two tools would fight over every run.
tools/ci_tooling/check/*_baseline.json
tools/ci_tooling/check/check_test_coverage_baseline.json

# Measured output, written by the generators that produce it.
docs/footprints.json
docs/feature_ranges.json

# Upstream test vectors, curated out of a pinned checkout by tools/crypto/curate_crypto_vectors.py
# (json.dump, indent=1). Their shape is the curator's, not Prettier's, or the two rewrite each
# other on every refresh.
test/vectors/

# npm owns the lockfile's shape.
package-lock.json

# Editor and agent state, untracked and not the repo's source.
.vscode/

# The theme CSS and the favicon SVGs are written by src/web_assets/wizard/gen_themes.py and
# gen_favicons.py, and Feature Tables regenerates and commits them, so Prettier would lose to the
# next run. src/web_assets/input/ is NOT here: those are hand-edited, and build_assets.py minifies
# them into the served string, so their formatting never reaches a blob. The pre-commit hook
# formats them on purpose.
src/web_assets/themes/
src/web_assets/favicons/
# A response template, not a document: the {{uptime_ms}} placeholders are substituted at serve
# time, so it does not parse as JSON and Prettier errors rather than formatting it.
src/web_assets/input/PROTOCORE_STATS_JSON.json

# Generated pages: gen_configurator.py and gen_features_page.py own these.
docs/configurator.html
docs/features.html

# Doxygen's own templates. The $token substitutions and the <!--BEGIN ...--> conditional markers
# are line-oriented, and reflowing them breaks the generated site rather than the file.
docs/footer.html
docs/header.html
